//
// A double IS m * 2^e with m an integer below 2^53, so its Rational is exact and needs
// NO bit access: scaling a double by a power of two is exact provided you never
// overflow and never enter the subnormals, and the loops below are driven so they
// do not. (1.5).to_r is (3/2).
//
// A double denominator holds 2^-e only while -e <= 1023; below about 2^-971 the
// denominator is built as a big.
//
// An infinity or a NaN has no Rational: MRI raises FloatDomainError, and without
// the guard rbGcd would run `x % y` with y = NaN forever. The twins are ratOfFlo
// in ruby-interpreter.abnf and rubyRatOfFlo in abnf/jsrt.go.
