// __-prefixed slot - so the copy cannot pick the singleton slots up by
// accident, which is the trap the Go twin's generic clone falls into: it walks
// o.keys RAW. The one difference between the two IS those slots: #clone keeps the
// singleton class, #dup drops it, and the tables are COPIED rather than shared so a
// def on the clone does not reach the original.
